  "title": "Covered calls and cash-secured puts trade upside for stability",
  "summary": "Cash-secured puts and covered calls work well when implied volatility is rich relative to realized volatility, and when you want to give up upside for a steadier portfolio. They are not the right trades if your goal is to maximize total return, because the short call or put caps the gain.",
